073,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b><span style=\"font-size:28px\">CHRONICLES OF DARKNESS</span><br /> <br /> GAME CHRONICLES</b></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B9w_tLv7Inayalh6S0JIOW5aSUk/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A Wheel of Fear and Fate</a> - </b>Last Update: June 23, 2017</span><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/WtD2wnw.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>(ABANDONED: 41 PAGES)</b><br /> <br /> <i><b>This is my first attempt at storytelling Chronicles of Darkness. Unfortunately it seems like this project will never be finished because we stopped playing the game before we could complete the story. Hopefully you will still get some enjoyment out of it.</b></i><br /> <br /> The small town of Chime is nearly forgotten in Jackson County, Oregon. A hundred years ago, it was known as the greatest manufacturer of grandfather clocks in the United States, much due to the machine created by its founder Arthur D. Chime. This machine was often called the god of all machines, and it was the cause of both blessings and tragedies in the small town. Eventually it was shut down and the factory was turned into a museum. Today, a hundred years later, the machine has woken up as if from a hundred year's slumber, and it calls upon the people of Chime to repair it, so that it can return to its former glory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":482,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","user":"Ekorren","date":". 04-06-2018, 10:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/mem